    <task><title>Part 1: Evaluate the limit</title>
<statement><p>Evaluate the following limit by simplifying the expression (first answer box) and then evaluating the limit (second answer box).</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \lim_{x\to 7} {\frac{x^{2}-49}{x-7}} = \lim_{x\to 7} }</m> <fillin characters="17" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>\displaystyle{= }</m> <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0002"/>.</p>
<p>Note: In your written solution, you should write the limit statement <m>\displaystyle{\lim_{x \to 7}}</m> in every step except the last one, where the limit is finally evaluated.</p>
</statement><answer><p><m>x+7</m></p></answer><answer><p><m>14</m></p></answer></task>
    <task><title>Part 2: Follow-up question</title>
<statement><p><m>\displaystyle{ \lim_{x\to 7} \frac{ x - 7 }{ \sqrt{x} - \sqrt{7} } = \lim_{x\to 7} }</m> <fillin characters="17" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>\displaystyle{= }</m> <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0004"/>.</p>
<p>Hint: Think of <m>x-7</m> as a difference of squares and factor it, or use the <lq/>conjugate trick<rq/>.</p>
</statement><answer><p><m>\sqrt{x}+2.64575</m></p></answer><answer><p><m>5.2915</m></p></answer></task>
